    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • 2026 Paris Motor Show: Jeep Reveals Six-Model European Strategy for 2030, Renegade Is Set to Return\nMercedes-AMG F1 Drivers George Russell and Kimi Antonelli Go Off-Road in BMW-Powered SUVs\n7 photos\nPhoto: INEOS\nThere's a certain irony whenever a Formula 1 driver gets behind the wheel of something a lot more rudimentary like an old-school 4x4. I quite like it. It speaks to their character. Anyway, that's exactly what's going on in this new INEOS campaign, where Mercedes-AMG F1 drivers George Russell and Kimi Antonelli got the chance to experience the Grenadier in its natural habitat.\nThe carmaker just released a new promotional video featuring George and Kimi behind the wheel of the Grenadier 4x4, each with their own build/spec of the vehicle. Antonelli went with a roof rack, hard shell tent, a Batwing awning and tailgate table, so that he can enjoy a little tiramisu along the way. This is what's called a camp-ready spec.\nMeanwhile, George's build was a trail-ready spec with a recovery kit, rock sliders, a bull bar, and Gearmate drawers for his essentials, meaning his padel gear. By the way, if you purchase your INEOS Grenadier now, you will receive a complimentary kit of your choice up to £3,536 ($4,720). Basically the Expedition kit, Cargo kit, and the Field kit are all in play. The latter is a £2,376 ($3,171) option.\nAs part of the marketing ad, Russell and Antonelli are filmed taking a detour from the tarmac and pulling in for an unusual pit stop - or rather a 'Grid Stop'. That's where the Grenadier pit crew quickly mounts all the fitting accessories, camping kit and custom enhancements. Like I said, it's all tongue-in-cheek and meant to highlight how the Grenadier can be customized to suit pretty much every buyer's specific needs and preferences.\n\"The INEOS Grenadier is built for more, designed to give owners the freedom to customize their vehicle to fit whatever their 'more' may be. With a dash of humor and the two hottest drivers in Formula 1, the 'Grid Stop' film shows that customization possibilities are endless. We hope it inspires everyone watching to kit out their own Grenadier,\" stated INEOS' chief marketing officer, Jonathan Hill.\nAs some of you probably know already, INEOS is a major partner for Mercedes- AMG in F1, not to mention a one-third shareholder in the team. It's only natural that they would go above and beyond to promote this partnership. In fact, INEOS has been a Mercedes F1 partner since 2020, and while the Grenadier is closely associated with Mercedes through this partnership, there's something quite amusing going on here.\nPhoto: INEOS The Grenadier is powered by BMW engines. That's right. What you're seeing here are two Mercedes F1 drivers helping promote a vehicle powered by engines sourced from one of their employer's biggest rivals in the passenger car segment. Not that there's anything wrong with that. I'm just saying... it's amusing. Besides, the Grenadier was never intended to compete with any luxury SUVs from Mercedes-Benz to begin with.\nThis is more of a spiritual successor to the original Land Rover Defender, putting the focus on durability and off-road capability.\nI quite like it. I didn't think I would, initially. But I've long since come around to it.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nineos grenadier ineos Grenadier Mercedes-AMG F1 team Mercedes-AMG george russell Kimi Antonelli\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Sergiu Tudose\nSergiu got to experience both American and European car \"scenes\" at an early age (his father drove a Ford Fiesta XR2 supermini in the 80s). After spending over 15 years at local and international auto publications, he's starting to appreciate comfort behind the wheel more than raw power and acceleration. Full profile\nUP NEXT Spy Photos: 2027 or 2028 Land Rover Range Rover Reveals New Details As It Starts Losing Camouflage",
